{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Nīta","html":"<article id='thag1.84'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.84 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.84 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Navamavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Nine </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Nītattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Nīta </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Sabbarattiṁ supitvāna, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sleeping all night, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>divā saṅgaṇike rato; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>happily socializing by day, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kudāssu nāma dummedho, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>when will the simpleton </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>dukkhassantaṁ karissatī”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>make an end of suffering? </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Nīto thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
